Intermittent HTTP 502 / ICAP error through proxy when connecting to ServiceNow API

We are seeing intermittent connectivity failures from an OpenShift application when connecting to the ServiceNow API through the corporate proxy.

Target endpoint: .servicenowservices.com/oauth_token.do

The application uses the configured corporate proxy on port 8080.

Some requests are successful and return HTTP 200, but other requests with the same configuration intermittently return HTTP 502.

During the failure, the response is coming back as an ICAP error:



Because the request fails at this point, the ServiceNow OAuth request does not return an access token and the application cannot continue.

We have confirmed that successful and failed requests are using the same OpenShift environment, application image, ServiceNow endpoint, credentials configuration, and proxy configuration. The issue is intermittent — the same request can return HTTP 200 and later return HTTP 502.

please review the proxy/ICAP logs and investigate why requests to the ServiceNow endpoint are intermittently failing with HTTP 502 / ICAP internal error?

For Business Impact, put:

This application automates processing of ServiceNow change requests and change tasks for OpenShift deployments. When the proxy/ICAP request fails, ServiceNow authentication cannot complete and the automated processing is interrupted.
